t as method of waste disposal (AOR = 4.91; 95\% CI: 1.39-13.29) and use of  soap for hand washing (AOR = 2.89; 95\% CI: 1.35-6.15) were significantly associated  with childhood diarrhea. Moreover, 30\% of sampled water from cases and 26\% of  sampled water from controls families were free from Escherichia coli whereas all  sampled water analyzed for Total coliforms were positive. CONCLUSIONS: We conclude  that the main sources of drinking water, hand washing before water drawing from a  storage container, domestic waste disposal place and use of soap for hand washing  were the most important factors for the prevention of childhood diarrhea.},
